        "#UK Consumer Credit Risk Analysis and Predictive Modelling\n",
        "\n",
        "##**Project** **Overview**\n",
        "\n",
        "This project investigates UK consumer credit trends and applies predictive modelling techniques to explore borrower default risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis combines Bank of England consumer credit statistics and Credit Conditions Survey data with a synthetic dataset of 5,000 fictional borrowers.\n",
        "\n",
        "The main objectives are to:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Analyse trends in UK consumer credit outstanding.\n",
        "* Investigate changes in unsecured credit availability and default indicators.\n",
        "* Explore borrower affordability using financial ratios.\n",
        "* Develop a probability of default (PD) framework.\n",
        "* Train a logistic regression model to classify simulated default outcomes.\n",
        "* Evaluate model performance and investigate classification thresholds.\n",
        "\n",
        "Tools: Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn and Scikit-learn.\n",
        "\n",
        "Important data distinction: The Bank of England datasets contain published economic and lending statistics. The individual borrower records and their default outcomes are synthetically generated for this project."
      ],
