        "**Interpretation** **of** **Consumer** **Credit** **Trends**\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset contains 69 monthly observations, with no missing values.\n",
        "\n",
        "Consumer credit outstanding increased from approximately £200.1 billion in January 2021 to £261.2 billion in September 2026.\n",
        "\n",
        "The year-on-year increase in September 2026 was approximately 7.43%.\n",
        "\n",
        "This indicates an overall increase in outstanding household consumer credit over the period. However, an increase in outstanding balances does not necessarily indicate an increase in defaults. Further information on arrears, repayments and default rates would be needed to assess borrower repayment performance."
      ],
