        "##**Borrower Affordability and Financial Ratios**\n",
        "\n",
        "Three financial ratios were calculated to examine borrower debt commitments relative to income.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Debt-to-Income (DTI) = Existing debt divided by annual income.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Monthly Debt-to-Income = Monthly debt repayments divided by gross monthly income.\n",
        "\n",
        "Loan-to-Income (LTI) = Requested loan amount divided by annual income.\n",
        "\n",
        "These ratios provide different perspectives on borrower indebtedness and affordability. Higher ratios may indicate greater financial commitments relative to income and potentially increased credit risk."
      ],
