      "source": [
        "##**Probability of Default (PD) Framework**\n",
        "\n",
        "A borrower-level risk score was developed using selected credit and affordability characteristics.\n",
        "\n",
        "The variables included:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Credit score.\n",
        "* Number of missed payments.\n",
        "* Debt-to-income ratio.\n",
        "* Monthly debt-to-income ratio.\n",
        "* Unemployment status.\n",
        "\n",
        "These variables were combined using specified coefficients to calculate a risk score.\n",
        "\n",
        "A logistic function was then applied to convert the risk score into a probability between 0 and 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "This creates a probability of default (PD) estimate for each synthetic borrower. For this project, the PD is treated as an assumed 12-month probability.\n",
        "\n",
        "The coefficients and baseline were selected for the simulation rather than estimated from historical default data. Therefore, the resulting PDs are not calibrated estimates of real-world borrower default risk."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Iz5Z_zZh94FP"
      }
    },
