        "**Simulated Default Outcomes**\n",
        "\n",
        "The probability of default estimates were used to generate binary default outcomes for the 5,000 synthetic borrowers.\n",
        "\n",
        "A value of 1 represents a simulated default, while 0 represents no simulated default.\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset produced 723 simulated defaults, representing a default rate of 14.46%.\n",
        "\n",
        "Borrowers assigned a simulated default had:\n",
        "\n",
        "* A lower average credit score (608.74 compared with 655.54).\n",
        "* Higher average debt-to-income ratios (45.05% compared with 26.57%).\n",
        "* Higher average monthly debt-to-income ratios (30.21% compared with 18.55%).\n",
        "\n",
        "These differences are consistent with the assumptions used to generate the simulated probabilities and outcomes. They should not be interpreted as independently established relationships from actual borrower data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FBQ74vrM-gPI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##**Logistic Regression Model**\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic regression was selected as a classification method to predict borrower default outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "The target variable is the binary Default column:\n",
        "\n",
        "* 1 = simulated default.\n",
        "* 0 = no simulated default.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model uses borrower demographic, financial and credit-related characteristics as input features.\n",
        "\n",
        "The simulated probability of default and risk score were excluded from the model features because they were used to generate the default outcomes. Including them would introduce target leakage and allow the model to use information directly involved in constructing its target variable."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fu_oPkQS-m6R"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "features= [\n",
        "           \"Age\",\n",
        "           \"Annual_Income\",\n",
        "           \"Credit_Score\",\n",
        "           \"Existing_Debt\",\n",
        "           \"Loan_Amount\",\n",
        "           \"Loan_Term_Months\",\n",
        "           \"Missed_Payments\",\n",
        "           \"Employment_Status\",\n",
        "           \"Monthly_Debt_Payments\",\n",
        "           \"Debt_to_Income_Ratio\",\n",
        "           \"Monthly_Debt_to_Income_Ratio\",\n",
        "           \"Loan_to_Income_Ratio\"\n",
        "          ]\n",
        "\n",
        "X = borrowers[features]\n",
        "y = borrowers[\"Default\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Features shape:\", X.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Target shape:\", y.shape)"
      ],
